# rocprofiler-compute (AI)

This project is **rocprofiler-compute** under `projects/rocprofiler-compute` in rocm-systems. The harness is **multi-model**; see [`.ai/harness/multi_model.md`](../../.ai/harness/multi_model.md).

## Four layers (same as Codex / Claude / Copilot)

1. **Context** — [`.ai/rules/core.md`](../../.ai/rules/core.md) + optional [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) / [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md).
2. **Skills** — One playbook from [`.ai/skills/index.md`](../../.ai/skills/index.md); navigate with [`.ai/harness/capabilities.md`](../../.ai/harness/capabilities.md).
3. **Tools** — [`.ai/harness/tools-policy.md`](../../.ai/harness/tools-policy.md) for bash, git, pytest, CMake.
4. **Hooks** — Run pre-commit / `python3 scripts/ai_dev_harness.py` before push when possible.

## Required

- **Rules** — `.ai/rules/core.md`, `.ai/rules/security.md`, `.ai/rules/anti_patterns.md`, and `.ai/rules/profiling_infra.md` when touching traces/metrics/roofline.
- **Standards** — `.ai/standards/python.md`, `cpp.md`, or `cmake.md` for touched languages.
- **Scope** — Small, single-purpose diffs; no new dependencies unless explicitly requested and approved.

## Verify

- Python: `ruff check`, `ruff format` per `pyproject.toml`; `pytest` for behavior changes.
- C++/CMake: out-of-source configure/build for `src/lib/` targets.

## If unclear

Ask instead of guessing (ROCm APIs, trace formats, counter names). Use `.ai/prompts/default.md` when helpful.

Full map: `.ai/README.md` and `docs/AI_GUIDE.md`.
